def _limits():
    return [
        H2("8.11 Limitations of the results"),
        B("**Synthetic training data.** The decision-model figures describe a generated corpus. They are not evidence of the ability to predict real editorial decisions, and the model's output on real papers (all borderline) shows it.",
          "**Small, team-written probe set.** Forty abstracts, six reviewers and labels written by the same team that built the matcher. The top-1 of 0.95 is an upper-bound style figure for a friendly sample, not an estimate for a real conference.",
          "**Demo reviewer pool.** Six invented profiles; no publication histories, no h-index and no real workloads. Behaviour with hundreds of real reviewers was measured for time only, not for quality.",
          "**No independent expert judgement and no user study.** Nobody outside the team rated the rankings, the structural scores or the language-model reviews.",
          "**Novelty is not assessed.** The Novelty bar is a fixed 55; the literature tab is context, and it can return the paper itself.",
          "**One machine, one run per timing.** Latencies come from a single CPU-only PC; the full-analysis times are single runs and vary by tens of seconds with other load.",
          "**Heuristic structural score.** Its weights were chosen by the team, not fitted; three of its four components barely move for ordinary papers.",
          "**Not measured at all:** accuracy on real peer-review decisions, scanned PDFs, non-English papers, GPU speed, concurrent users, and the quality of the language-model review as judged by people."),
    ]


